    <region left="0" top="1287" width="605" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>In simply supported beams, I.e is calculated based on the mid-span value. For continuous beam, a<br />weighted average of the support and span is more appropriate due to the varying degree of cracking<br />at these two regions. The weighted average I.e is calculated from :</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="432" top="1332" width="32" height="29" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">I.em</e>
        </input>
      </math>
    </region>
